* ============================================================================
* descend_seek_probe.dts -- PROBE (not a regression) for the unattributed BBS
* report "descending path looks off" (board.afb.chat thread 'seek',
* [unattributed history]; triaged by the AIF-108 mail read 2026-08-12).
* Probe-before-number discipline: an AIF is claimed only if this reads red.
*
* Shape: self-bootstrapping disposable x64 table in the RAM VFS (nothing on
* disk, self-erasing on unmount). Build a CNX tag -- CNX is the ONLY valid
* index lane in RAM (owner ruling 2026-08-12; INDEX ON builds an INX via
* std::ofstream, which bypasses the ramfs and dies on the virtual indexes
* dir -- same bypass family as the DTX memo sidecar). Bootstrap sequence is
* prior art from cnx_realtime_index_proof.dts: CNX CREATE / CNX ADDTAG /
* REBUILD / SET ORDER TAG. Measure BY FIELD VALUE with ALLTRIM (the IDXSTALE
* lesson: RECNO()/FOUND() render empty in ? markers) what ASCEND/DESCEND
* actually do to traversal and SEEK.
*
* Version note: v1 of this probe used INDEX ON ... TAG in RAM; every marker
* read .F. because the INX write failed and no order ever existed -- an
* invalid run, not a red. This v2 is the corrected scaffold.
*
* VERDICT (run 2026-08-12, build Aug 11 2026 18:37:52 c78c8bd1): ALL GREEN,
* DS_G0 + DS_T1..T6 = .T. Descending traversal, BOTTOM-under-descend,
* SEEK-under-descend, and ASCEND restore are correct on a live CNX order in
* the RAM VFS. The BBS report "descending path looks off" is CLOSED with
* evidence -- no AIF claimed (probe-before-number held).
*
* Scaffold observation banked from the green run (ramfs-bypass ledger,
* member 3): CNX CREATE lands in the ramfs, but CNX ADDTAG and REBUILD
* existence-check the REAL filesystem and report "CNX not found" for a file
* the VFS holds. SET ORDER's CNX fallback then attaches a realtime-
* maintained order anyway, which is what the markers measured. Members 1-2:
* DTX memo sidecar (spec 38 correction), INX writer (v1 of this probe).
*
* Markers:
*   DS_G0 guard: SEEK works at all (order is live) -- if G0 is red the run
*         is invalid and T1-T6 prove nothing (the v1 lesson, made a marker)
*   DS_T1 ascending TOP is the minimum key
*   DS_T2 ascending BOTTOM is the maximum key
*   DS_T3 after DESCEND, TOP is the MAXIMUM key (the reversed traversal)
*   DS_T4 after DESCEND, BOTTOM is the minimum
*   DS_T5 SEEK an existing middle key under DESCEND still lands on it
*   DS_T6 back to ASCEND, TOP is the minimum again (state restores)
* If DS_T3/DS_T4/DS_T5 read .F., the 5-word report was right and the red is
* the finding -- record values, claim a number, write the regression.
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

DO mem
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO mem

FORMULA "DESCEND-PROBE-BEGIN"

CREATE X64 DSPROBE (ID N(8,0), NAME C(12))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 30
REPLACE NAME WITH "CHARLIE"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 10
REPLACE NAME WITH "ALPHA"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 50
REPLACE NAME WITH "ECHO"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 20
REPLACE NAME WITH "BRAVO"
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 40
REPLACE NAME WITH "DELTA"

CNX CREATE
CNX ADDTAG NAME
REBUILD
SET ORDER TAG NAME

* --- G0: the order is LIVE before anything is asserted about direction ------
GO 4
SEEK "CHARLIE"
? "DS_G0_order_is_live:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "CHARLIE")

TOP
? "DS_T1_asc_top_is_min:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "ALPHA")
BOTTOM
? "DS_T2_asc_bottom_is_max:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "ECHO")

DESCEND
TOP
? "DS_T3_desc_top_is_max:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "ECHO")
BOTTOM
? "DS_T4_desc_bottom_is_min:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "ALPHA")

SEEK "CHARLIE"
? "DS_T5_desc_seek_lands:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "CHARLIE")

ASCEND
TOP
? "DS_T6_asc_restored:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "ALPHA")

FORMULA "DESCEND-PROBE-END"

VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
